								<br>
								<strong><span style="font-size: 16px;">Capable * Creative * Conscientious * Confidential <br />
</span></strong><br />
Brent Rice has humbly served others as a commercial and residential Realtor/Broker and mortgage specialist for over 25 years. Brent is a creative minded professional who possesses the character, conscience and capacity to handle a wide range of real estate services including acquisition, disposition, leasing, management, consulting, analysis, strategic planning, and due diligence as well as financing virtually any type of real estate. With his in-depth understanding of the decision criteria and operation of commercial and residential properties, Brent has provided contract underwriting to a variety of financial institutions nationwide. Brent has extensive corporate experience as well as an entrepreneurial mind and spirit. He represents private clients with the utmost discretion and privacy of information. Brent distinguishes himself by consulting directly with clients and/or their financial advisors while remaining accessible throughout the transaction.Brent Rice's clients include business owners, professional athletes, corporate executives, and celebrities. His other interests include private aircraft (whole and fractional) consulting and finance as well as residential and commercial real estate investing. As a graduate of Texas Tech University, Brent Rice earned a BBA degree in Finance-Real Estate, holds a Texas Real Estate Broker's License, is a certified National Association of Realtors&reg; Short Sales and Foreclosure Resource (SFR) and is currently pursuing a CCIM designation. Brent is an avid golfer, basketball shooting instructor and&nbsp;worked as&nbsp;the official game clock operator of the 2011 World Champion,&nbsp;Dallas Mavericks' stat crew from January 2000 to August 2012.
